<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSE SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSE SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the third</p>
<p>day of four-day English county championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Friday:</p>
<p>At Derby: No play first two days. Surrey 267 (G.Thorpe 83,</p>
<p>M.P Bicknell 74; D E Malcolm 4-95), Derbyshire 113-2.</p>
<p>At Hartlepool: Nottinghamshire 170 and 68-2, Durham 331</p>
<p>(N.Speak 93, D.Boon 68)</p>
<p>At Bristol: Hampshire 316 and 46-3, Gloucestershire 403</p>
<p>(S.Young 73, J.Russell 66, M.Alleyne 62, M.Lynch 62; J P</p>
<p>Stephenson 4-81)</p>
<p>At Lord's: Middlesex 490-9 declared, Sussex 187 (W.Athey 60</p>
<p>not out; J.Hewitt 4-60) and 6-0.</p>
<p>At Northampton: Northamptonshire 185 and 104-3, Somerset 290</p>
<p>(G.Rose 109 not out, M.Burns 82; Mohammad Akram 5-72)</p>
<p>At Worcester: Worcestershire 257, Leicestershire 69 (P J</p>
<p>Newport 7-37) and 141-4 (N.Johnson 87 not out)</p>
<p>At Headingley: Glamorgan 336 (S.James 109, R.Croft 57, H</p>
<p>Morris 55; D Gough 5-56) and 27-0, Yorkshire 200-9 declared</p>
<p>(D.Lehmann 54; R.Croft 4-58).</p>
</text>
